// A book that writes no account with the entities that fill its slots before its name reads every reference as it did.
// A party written as a path that ends in an account's name (`clients/escrow`) or begins with an entity that fills a slot
// (`jordan/landlord`) is an implied party, and not a mistake in an address.
use std
base USD
entity jordan : person
account bank/escrow : deposit
account jordan-nest : deposit
  owner jordan
opening 2026-01-01
  bank/escrow 100 USD
  jordan-nest 100 USD
2026-02-01 clients/escrow -> bank/escrow 5 USD
2026-02-02 bank/escrow -> vendors/escrow 3 USD
2026-02-03 jordan-nest -> jordan/landlord 7 USD
